    {
      "id": "claim_fa1dcf56a4ff4bdab6977b6fa0e89869",
      "statement": "AGENTS.md section 2 defines a seven-level truth order: (1) owner instruction, (2) current docs/ Markdown plus smoke-tests/ acceptance authority when testing, (3) current live evidence from the server, (4) approved runbook/execution artifact, (5) governed HX wrapper skill plus vendor guidance, (6) historical/archive reference, (7) general model knowledge. Source code and tests are NOT in this list; they are evidence, not authority. If live evidence or vendor requirements contradict an active document, the document stops being sufficient proof and the contradiction must be reported.",
