    {
      "id": "claim_9c7f74f8dc2d4238a6046d1bfb4f920f",
      "statement": "The tools/hx-doc/ tools are the enforcement layer for written rules: hx-doc-check (links resolve, registry vocabulary defined, control frontmatter complete, filenames stable, evidence committable, and refuses generated blocks calling code/tests authoritative), hx-proof (proof DAG valid and generated blocks current), hx-render-html (every human-html/ mirror matches its Markdown source), hx-version-pins (pins current, no apt/Snap application), hx-upstream-drift (registry pinned commits still current), hx-record-check (server records follow template), hx-smoke-lint (smoke authorities carry required sections). CI runs them all; a failure is a real defect, not noise to bypass.",
